  "title": "Robodebt Algorithmic Injustice",
  "objective": "Simulate tensions between welfare recipients, frontline workers, and policymakers during Australia's unlawful automated debt recovery scheme",
  "brief": "Australia's Robodebt automated welfare debt recovery scheme (2016-2020). An algorithm averaged annual income across fortnights to generate false debts, issuing 500,000+ notices. A Royal Commission found it unlawful; the scheme caused documented suicides. Stakeholders: a single parent issued an incorrect $12K debt notice who cannot afford legal representation, a Centrelink call center worker processing appeals they know are unjust but face disciplinary action for raising concerns, a government data scientist who flagged the averaging algorithm flaws internally but was overruled, and a social worker counseling affected clients through financial and mental health crises caused by the notices.",
